WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.344
On the eve of the Battle of Red Cliffs, Zhou Yu deliberately made things hard for Zhuge Liang, demanding a hundred thousand arrows within ten days.

00:00:07.694 --> 00:00:14.918
Zhuge Liang smiled calmly and said three days would be enough — and he even signed a military pledge.

00:00:15.268 --> 00:00:22.540
On the morning of the third day, a thick fog rose over the river, and no figures could be seen across the water.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.234
The dense fog covered the river, and all around was quiet.

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:34.664
Zhuge Liang led twenty small boats bound full of straw men, quietly approaching Cao Cao's river camp.

00:00:35.014 --> 00:00:39.790
The war drums sounded again and again, their sound carrying far through the fog.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:48.276
Unable to see what was real, Cao Cao's army loosed volleys of arrows, which stuck into the straw men like raindrops.

00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:52.706
Before long, both sides of the straw boats were stuck full of arrows.

00:00:53.056 --> 00:01:00.184
Zhuge Liang returned with a full load; Zhou Yu welcomed him in person, completely convinced, praising him again and again.

